<h2>Frequently asked</h2>
<div class="faq-item">
  <h4>What's the difference between two-engine and full audit?</h4>
  <p>Two Engine Audit ($29) tests Google AI Overviews and ChatGPT — the two engines most buyers actually use today. Full audit ($79) adds Claude, Perplexity and Gemini for complete coverage. Start with two-engine if you're cost-sensitive; pick full if you want to be sure you're not missing visibility in a less-mainstream engine.</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
  <h4>Why monthly monitoring instead of just running another audit?</h4>
  <p>AI engines drift weekly. An audit is a snapshot in time. Monitoring re-runs the same audit every month so you can see trends — is your visibility improving or declining, which competitors are gaining ground, which sources keep getting cited. You also get a logged-in dashboard to add more brands or run on-demand audits.</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
  <h4>How is this different from a normal SEO audit?</h4>
  <p>Traditional SEO audits look at how Google's <em>blue links</em> rank. We measure how Google's AI Overview, ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity and Gemini <em>describe and recommend</em> you when buyers ask questions. That's a different game with different rules.</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
  <h4>Do results drift between runs?</h4>
  <p>Yes. AI answers vary day-to-day even with identical questions. The signal you should trust is the <em>pattern</em> — which engines mention you, which competitors keep showing up, which sources keep getting cited. That's why monitoring is more reliable than a single audit.</p>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
  <h4>What's your refund policy?</h4>
  <p>If the audit doesn't run successfully, you get a full automatic refund. If it runs and you don't find it useful, contact <a href="/support">support</a> within 14 days and we'll work something out. Monthly monitoring can be cancelled anytime — you keep access through the end of the current billing period.</p>
</div>
